# Permissions (device-layer-0001): whether the person has let the app use a capability, and asking them. Every
# capability that needs a grant asks through here, and the platform's own prompt is the only prompt.
#
#   names    camera, location, notification
#
#   permission-status(name)    granted, denied, not-determined (never asked), restricted (the device's owner or a
#                              policy decides), or unavailable (this platform has no such grant, or no such capability)
#   request-permission(name)   asks once, through the platform's prompt, and answers the status after it. Asking
#                              again after a refusal answers `denied` without a prompt, as every platform does
#
# A platform reads its usage declaration before it prompts (an iOS Info.plist string, an Android manifest permission),
# which the build writes for the capabilities an app reaches (device-layer-0012).

load ./native/{platform}/permission
  find read-permission
  find ask-permission

task permission-status
  take name, like text
  like text
  send back
    call read-permission
      read name

task request-permission
  take name, like text
  like text
  send back
    call ask-permission
      read name
